</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 6:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s ok Rocky I like your idea shows your normal lol. B. I have been stumped by this symbol and trying very hard, maybe to hard at this point to attach the meaning or his thinking at the time of it&#39;s creation. I agree with the sexual conotations behind the design, and feel that the preparation for children is a possibility, I would like, since you already started it and we have 8 thousand threads, to discuss this issue here if no one minds. I believe as most do that Rader was drawn to the work of the Zodiac, His pain and aggression due to who knows at this point, could have been pain in intercourse, could have been a victim of child molestation, Not sure right now. But Zodiac had that same problem, IE killing young couples and women who had previously turned him down. Anyway Rader could Identify with whatever it was. For Rader the notion of sexual agression came from seeing young girls, and if you look at Shirly, Stefinie Welch and Kerri you will see they all look alike, Kerri and Stefanie could be twins. Here is my problem when Rader killed Joseph Otero and please do not ask where I got this from, but we all said it must have been bad because of what the cop said, I believe the Three hoods, where a symbol meaning the opposite of the genital circumcision that all young boys have. So I think he also cut off the boys penis, I hate to be so to the point. but this is the only way I can explain. The boy would not have to suffer the pains of male adulthood. I believe the combination of Sexual aggression and not being able to live up to his role as a man, and of course his sociopathic tendencies, drew him at a very young age to the Zodiac. Someone who could share his pain. I also feel that if LE had the time to go search areas Rader ventured off too, that they would find a hiding place, not the shed but underground, old coal shaft or closed mine, because of the train idea, that they wuld find his comic books, drawings and trophies from this obsession that he has had for a very very long time. Might Sound odd but I feel like Ted Bundy and the others, That Rader was not really a breast man, The symbol represted what he hated most, being contoled by the sexual drive he had when he saw women, That is why he tied them up, so he would not have them touching him. He hid in the church becuase for some reason he thought that might stop some of this need, or uncontrolable sexual aggression.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
