<!--Post: 11821--><!--Time: 1111221742-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11821"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 12:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->People, you are not going to believe this - this is WAY COOL!  We were right about this symbol – everything.  Holy cow!  Somebody wake up Johno.  &#40;Embersage, you never sleep anyway!&#41;  Check this out...... <BR> <BR>It&#39;s a friggin&#39; ZODIAC symbol! <BR> <BR>Turn on Unicode encoding in your browser and follow along.... <BR> <BR>I was having lunch today with my Japanese langauage contact &#40;who gave me a translation of a cold case in Japan for Verm_inve&#41;.  I showed her the BTK symbol, drawn in the usual way, but without eyes &#40;meaning turned with the B facing down, like glasses or breasts, like we&#39;ve all been drawing it all along&#41;.  She said there are no kanji with that curved part of the B, which makes sense because of the straight strokes used for Chinese characters &#40;i.e., the Japanese kanji&#41;, except in calligraphy. <BR> <BR>Anyway, then I said “how about if the “B” part was squared off, like a horizonal domino, meaning two squares side-by-side, sitting on top of the “T-K” part &#40;“ki”, 木&#41;?  Like a digital “8” on a cheap LED calculator &#40;2 squares joined&#41;, or like the rising sun symbol “nichi” &#40;日&#41; on its side, and then on top of the &#34;T-K&#34;.  She said that the two-square character is generally vertical when used in kanji, although it is occasionally seen horizonal &#40;more often the analogous three-square character is seen horizontal&#41;, but never in combination with the “ki” character.  Put more simply, she said that even squaring off the “B” in the BTK symbol, it wasn&#39;t a real kanji.  The closest thing is the kanji for “chestnut” &#40;ritsu, 栗&#41;, which has a 3-square with an extra handle on top, resting on top of “ki”.  To wit, a 3-eyed BTK symbol with alien granny glasses.  Negative. <BR> <BR>Then I drew her the character that Johno pointed out on the web page, that he thought looked like the BTK symbol &#40;味&#41;.  That character in Japanese is called “mi”, and means “taste”, and consists of two parts.  The elongated square on the left generally means “mouth” &#40;“ko”, 口, usually more squared when alone, more compressed when combined&#41;, and the BTK-symbol-looking thing &#40;未&#41;, which is like “ki” with an extra bar on top, is also called “mi” &#40;go figure&#41;, and is used to mean “future”, “still”, or “not yet” in combination with other symbols. <BR> <BR>Here&#39;s the cool part.  She said &#40;nearly verbatim&#41;, “We never use that part by itself in Japanese regular writing.  It only used in Japanese Zodiac.  It used for &#39;year of sheep&#39;, or &#39;year of lamb&#39; or &#39;year of ram&#39; &#40;未年, hitsujidoshi&#41;, not regular Japanese kanji for sheep.”  I asked her 3 times just to make absolutely sure what she was saying, and then I wrote it down.   Zodiac.  Zodiac.  Zodiac. <BR> <BR>Sure enough, if you go out on the web, you will find that there are two different characters used for the Year of the Sheep in the Chinese and Japanese Zodiacs.  The common word used for the animal in normal conversation is the one that looks like it has horns &#40;羊&#41;, but the more traditional one used in the Asian Zodiac is basically the BTK symbol without the curve of the B or the dots for eyes &#40;未&#41;.  It&#39;s called “hitsuji” in Japanese, and the year of the sheep is called “hitsujidoshi” &#40;未年, sheep year&#41;. <BR> <BR>The Years of the Sheep are:  1907, 1919, 1931, 1943, 1955, 1967, 1979, 1991, 2003.  You guys are the Zodiac and BTK timeline experts – you figure it out.  I&#39;m just a language and code guy.  Maybe you can make sense of why he chose it, other than he could fit his name into it. <BR> <BR>Here are some web sites.  Check &#39;em out: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.takase.com/Zodiac/Astrology.htm" target=_top>http://www.takase.com/Zodiac/Astrology.htm</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://asnic.utexas.edu/asnic/countries/china/czod.html" target=_top>http://asnic.utexas.edu/asnic/countries/china/czod .html</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.onmarkproductions.com/html/8-zodiac-protectors.shtml" target=_top>http://www.onmarkproductions.com/html/8-zodiac-pro tectors.shtml</a> <BR> <BR>It all makes sense.  You can morph “hitsuji” into the BTK symbol by merely drawing the curves of the B on it, and touching up the top part of the center line a bit with an eraser, so it&#39;s not too obvious what it is.  In reality, he spaced the lines a little extra-wide to make the B scale properly, and to accent the boobs, but that&#39;s pretty much it.  All along I was thinking it was just some dopey junior-high doodle, when in reality it was a surprisingly sophisticated Zodiac “homage” symbol.  The boobs are really far less of a message than a diversion or a camouflage.  I have a secret symbol for my initials, which a few people know and which they generally think is pretty clever.  I would say that BTK&#39;s is just as thoughtful. <BR> <BR>All this time I thought that you Zodiac/BTK linkers were pushing the margins a little hard.  Heck, now we know.  BTK was a total Zodiac fan-boy.  You guys had him pegged from go.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11821-->
<!--Post: 11844--><!--Time: 1111276502-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11844"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 3:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I will Kiss you Pax, when I see you lol <BR>Here is a message for you from Canada <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.c-c-c.org/chineseculture/zodiac/Rooster.htm" target=_top>http://www.c-c-c.org/chineseculture/zodiac/Rooster .htm</a> <BR>  <BR>This is the year of the rooster  2005 - also, wasn&#39;t Rader born in 1945 another year of the rooster. <BR>  <BR>The site may provide other insight into BTK&#39;s Zodiac symbol. <BR>  <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11844-->
<!--Post: 11856--><!--Time: 1111280891-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11856"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 5:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK like the Zodiac was a copycat. The Zodiac sent a card with very distinct looking symbols which were thought to be some sort of chinese characters to the press.  <BR> <BR>One rather disrespected author pointed out the similarities between the characters on the Zodiac card to symbols on a barrel that was recovered from one of the Santa Rosa hitchhiker murders of the 1970s which remain unsolved. <BR> <BR>BTK most likely has many more victims we are unaware of much like his &#34;hero&#34; the Zodiac.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11856-->
<!--Post: 11859--><!--Time: 1111281522-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11859"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 5:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes and you also need to take into consideration The original Night Stalker and what he has to do with these symbols<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11859-->
<!--Post: 11860--><!--Time: 1111282195-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11860"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 5:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I can explain one obvious thing to you right now, these years you have put down fall under the sign on the Ram which is my and&#40; Raders Birth sign&#41; we are Aries, the leader and the RAm<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11860-->
<!--Post: 11865--><!--Time: 1111303075-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11865"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 11:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pax56, I&#39;m awake and ready to report for duty so here goes. <BR> <BR>The year of the sheep symbol is very close and it is Zodiac. <BR>Btk was into the Zodiac and likely looked into the Zodiac&#39;s symbol and communications to find inspiration for his own symbol. <BR> <BR>&#34;She went to slaughter like a lamb.&#34; <BR>From &#39;The Confession&#39; sent anonomously to the Riverside, California Enterprise newspaper on November 19, 1966 describing the murder of Cheri Jo Bates. <BR> <BR>The murder and communication is long believed by many to be the earlist known murder and communication from a killer who would late become known in the San Fransico Bay area as The Zodiac. <BR>BTK being a regular church going man liked the lamb reference and looked for the zodiac symbol for the year of the lamb and found that in the Chinese zodiac there is no year of the lamb but rather the year of the sheep. When he saw the symbol he turned it side ways and saw a TK in it. He added the B to it and there he had his symbol. <BR>He was not a good shepherd, he was an evil shepherd. <BR> He would watch over the lambs and then lead them to slaughter. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11865-->
<!--Post: 11869--><!--Time: 1111305214-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11869"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 11:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Number 8 was not.&#34; <BR>From &#39;Oh Anna Why Didn&#39;t You Appear&#39; poem sent to intended victim Anna Williams by BTK June 15, 1979. <BR> <BR>The Sheep or The Lamb is the eighth sign of Chinese zodiac. <BR> <BR>Anna Williams was not intended to be murder victim number 8. BTK didn&#39;t mean eight in reference to us assuming that he had already killed seven people and Anna would have been the eighth. <BR> He was refering to the zodiac which inspired his secret symbol. <BR> <BR>In other words, One of my sheep she was not.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11869-->
<!--Post: 11884--><!--Time: 1111352457-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11884"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 1:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wow, Johno, the more I hear about Zodiac, the more I see the connection.  Rader truly was the &#34;Bad Shepherd&#34;.   Have there been any other &#34;students&#34; of Zodiac?  I guess I&#39;m wondering how common it is for serial killers to emulate each other in some sort of an evil fraternity.  Maybe there&#39;s no such thing as a &#34;copycat&#34; - that these guys just naturally do it, and when we say &#34;copycat&#34;, it&#39;s almost more reflective of our disgust in their mutual self-admiration, than it is in saying that one of them is less inventive than another, and therefore &#34;less&#34; of an SK.  Maybe the original ones are the atypical ones. <BR> <BR>Thanks, Ember.  I do think it&#39;s ironic that he was born and captured in a Rooster year.  A &#34;cocky&#34; rooster, clucking and crowing at the media, does seem to be his symbol, and the lamb &#40;sheep&#41; does befit the innocent victims.  Wouldn&#39;t you know it, I&#39;m a monkey - with all those &#34;monkey issues&#34;.  As a geek and a Christian, I don&#39;t put too much stock in this astrological stuff, but it&#39;s rather weird how it fits sometimes. <BR> <BR>I wonder, when more of Rader&#39;s communications are eventually released, if there will be more lamb and sheep references that will bolster this interpretation of his symbol.  It wouldn&#39;t surprise me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11884-->
<!--Post: 11889--><!--Time: 1111358629-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11889"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 2:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno and Pax, I am greatful that someone else has started realizing the importance of the Zodiac as it fits to Rader, Zodiac, The Night Stalker, I have something of worth to you both on this matter, yet it is to long to post, mail me asap for the link<!--/Text--></td></tr>
